2D Expect Privacy Policy

Effective Date: 20.10.2025

This Privacy Policy informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of Non-Personal Information we receive from users of the 2D Expect application (the "Service").

By using the Service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

1. Information Collection and Use

The Service is designed purely as a data viewer and does not collect any Personal Information that directly identifies you (like your name, email address, or phone number).

We only collect Non-Personal Data for the sole purpose of ensuring the app's stable operation and resolving technical issues.

1.1. Non-Personal Data (Automatically Collected)

We may automatically collect certain non-personal information when you use the Service:

    Device Information: This includes your device's model, operating system version, and unique identifiers (e.g., Device ID). This data is collected to ensure the app functions correctly across different devices and versions.

    Log Data (System Crash Logs): In case of a technical error or crash in the app, we collect data and information on your phone called Log Data. This may include information such as your device's Internet Protocol (“IP”) address, device name, operating system version, and the time and date of your use of the Service.

2. Use of Data

The Non-Personal Data collected is used exclusively for the following purposes:

    To provide and maintain the core Service (displaying the SET Index data).

    To monitor and analyze app stability and performance.

    To detect, prevent, and fix technical errors and crashes.

3. Data Sharing and Third-Party Disclosure

We value your privacy.

    We DO NOT use any third-party services for analytics, advertising (AdMob, etc.), or notifications (Firebase, etc.).

    We DO NOT sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your Non-Personal Data to outside parties.

    The only sharing of data that may occur is the transfer of the crash Log Data (as defined in 1.1) to our own internal secure server for troubleshooting purposes only.

4. Children's Privacy

Our Service does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13.

5. Security of Data

We take reasonable steps to protect the Non-Personal Data we collect from loss, misuse, and unauthorized access. However, no electronic storage is 100% secure.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

